      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original Wildwood City Hall, a two‑story brick building at 16962 Manchester Road, served the community from 1995 to 2009.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofwildwood.com/600/Grover",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elmer Funk owned the local general store and picnic area in 1921, turning it into a popular gathering spot for parades and band concerts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofwildwood.com/600/Grover",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Wetterer Smith Shop, built in 1865, later housed an interior design store and reflects Grover’s early commercial architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
